Z||000000||Formula88||12-30-2001||06:15 PM||||Ok, so who'd be interested in purchasing a copy of the Pontiac Fiero Parts CD (the P22 parts book)?<P>I'm not positng this on the Mall, because I don't have one for sale right now, but I want to see if there's interest.  I see them for sale on Ebay for $49 from time to time.  That's too much for a copied CD of acrobat documents, IMO.  I'll check into copyright issues and if it's not illegal, I'm willing to reproduce copies of it and sell to PFF members for $10 each, plus actual shipping charges.  Yeah, I'd probably also sell on Ebay for $40-50 if someone wanted to pay it, but the main goal is to get the valuable info to the Forum members who've helped me so much in the past.  Yes, I'd like to make some money, but at $10 each, you can tell money isn't my primary motivation.<P>So, anyone interested?  Post here if you are.  If there appears to be enough info, I'll check on production and let everyone know what I find out.<P>Here's the Ebay auction that inspired my post.  Hey, if you wanna bid on it, go ahead.  It's not my auction. <A HREF="http://cgi.ebay.com/aw-cgi/eBayISAPI.dll?ViewItem&item=1499556729" TARGET=_blank>http://cgi.ebay.com/aw-cgi/eBayISAPI.dll?ViewItem&item=1499556729</A> ||||reg||5
